{"claim":"Medigap plans cannot be objectively ranked best-to-worst because, per Medicare.gov, all plans sharing the same letter offer identical standardized benefits regardless of insurer, making price (not coverage quality) the key variable among same-letter plans.","status":"insufficient","reason":"Excerpts confirm same-letter plans have identical basic benefits and price is the differentiator among same-letter plans, but no excerpt supports the broader claim that plans cannot be 'objectively ranked best-to-worst' overall (across letters) based on this reasoning.","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.medicare.gov/health-drug-plans/medigap/basics","passage":"Price is the only difference between plans with the same letter that are sold by different insurance companies."}]}
{"claim":"Medicare.gov's official comparison chart shows coverage varies meaningfully across letters: e.g., Plans K and L require beneficiaries to meet an out-of-pocket limit ($8,000 for K, $4,000 for L in 2026) before the plan pays 100% of covered services for the rest of the year.","status":"insufficient","reason":"No excerpt provides the specific dollar amounts ($8,000 for K, $4,000 for L) or confirms 2026 figures; only general chart existence is mentioned.","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.medicare.gov/health-drug-plans/medigap/basics/compare-plan-benefits","passage":"The chart below shows what each Medigap plan covers for different Medicare services."}]}
{"claim":"Plan N is structured differently than full-coverage plans—it pays 100% of Part B coinsurance but requires copayments up to $20 for some office visits and up to $50 for ER visits that don't result in inpatient admission.","status":"insufficient","reason":"No excerpt describes Plan N's structure, copayment amounts for office or ER visits, or coverage of Part B coinsurance.","evidence":[]}
{"claim":"Official Medicare.gov sources confirm all Medigap plans with the same letter offer identical basic benefits regardless of insurer, so price/company is the main differentiator within a letter.","status":"supported","reason":"Directly supported by multiple excerpts confirming same-letter standardization and price as the key differentiator.","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.medicare.gov/health-drug-plans/medigap/basics","passage":"All Medigap policies are standardized. This means, policies with the same letter offer the same basic benefits no matter where you live or which insurance company you buy the policy from."},{"url":"https://www.medicare.gov/publications/11575-Getting-Started-Medicare-Supplement-Insurance.pdf#page=2","passage":"Price is the only difference between policies with the same letter sold by different companies."}]}
