{"claim":"Massachusetts does not use the standard lettered Medigap plan system (A-N); instead it offers three standardized plans: Core, Supplement 1, and Supplement 1A, each covering different combinations of Part A inpatient hospital deductible, Part A SNF coinsurance, Part B deductible, and foreign travel emergency benefits.","status":"insufficient","reason":"Excerpt confirms Massachusetts does not use the lettered system and lists basic benefits, but does not name or describe three specific plans called Core, Supplement 1, and Supplement 1A, nor their specific benefit coverage combinations.","evidence":[{"url":"https://www.medicare.gov/supplements-other-insurance/how-to-compare-medigap-policies/medigap-in-massachusetts","passage":"In Massachusetts, Medigap policies are standardized in a different way and offer these basic benefits: Inpatient hospital costs Medical costs Blood Part A hospice coinsurance or copayment"}]}
